        <item>
            <title>5.93</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:04:52 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>470</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>5.93</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2 style="font:600 15px -apple-system;margin:0 0 6px">Promptr Studio Pro 5.93</h2>
<p style="font:600 13px -apple-system;margin:0 0 4px">Smart Edit with Paul</p>
<ul style="font:13px -apple-system;margin:0;padding-left:18px">
<li><b>Paul switches the model for you.</b> Write “make this with Nano Banana Pro” or “use Kling 3 for this”, and Paul sets the composer to that model together with the prompt. If a model is not available right now or belongs to the other tab, he says so. Undo switches back and brings back the references the switch had to remove.</li>
<li><b>A character can have several images.</b> Paul brings up to three of them, the main image first, so the model sees more of the character than a single shot.</li>
<li><b>Assign images from the gallery.</b> Right-click one or more images to add them to a character Paul knows, or to create a new one.</li>
<li><b>All images of a character in one place.</b> The character window shows every image: choose the main image, remove one or add more from the Finder.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
